# Bootstrap wave 10 — the kube-agents per-cluster control plane (PINNED to a release ref). Rendered
# for @@CLUSTER@@.
#
# Pulls the operator's full install overlay (config/install): the Agent CRD, the controller-manager
# (RBAC + Deployment + cert-manager-issued webhook cert), the validating/mutating webhooks, the
# read-only kage-router (the ChatOps front door), and the mesh CA. Each cluster — hub or spoke — runs
# its own controller and router (05 §7: the controller reconciles ONLY its own cluster's Agent CRs).
#
# `config/install`, NOT `config/default`. `default` is the transformed half and omits the mesh CA,
# which cannot survive its `namePrefix`/`namespace` transformers. A cluster bootstrapped from
# `default` comes up with no trust root and every broker stuck waiting on an unsignable Certificate.
#
# Depends on wave 00 (cert-manager) for the webhook serving cert; the pipeline waits for the controller
# Deployment (kubeagents-controller-manager) to roll out before wave 20.
#
# PINNED to a git ref for reproducibility and a reviewable diff. Repin to a content-addressable digest
# (a tag that is immutable, or a commit SHA via ?ref=<sha>) for production. The router Deployment ships
# with placeholder KAGE_PROJECT_ID / KAGE_INBOUND_SUBSCRIPTION env — patch them per cluster or the router
# pod will fail fast until they are set.
apiVersion: kustomize.config.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Kustomization
resources:
  - github.com/gke-labs/kube-agents/k8s-operator/config/install?ref=v0.1.0
